  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RAD-05 and LAB-03. 8 original items plus 4 that arrived while I worked.\n\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram: no cause found for the hematuria. The incidental 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening. I first ordered a 12-month LDCT (sr-t0001). Then a Lakeshore addendum arrived (doc-06201): new 5 mm RUL nodule, Lung-RADS 3, LDCT at 6 months from 2026-04-14. Replaced with LDCT sr-t0031 (window ends 2026-11-14), tracking task task-t0032, corrected message to patient, note. I couldn't withdraw sr-t0001 or its tracking task task-t0002 with my tools; task-t0033 asks you to cancel them. Both items closed.\n- pt-0016 TSH: normal, closed. K 6.3: lab corrected it to 4.4 (analyzer error), closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, ED CTA (preliminary read): the final report says no PE and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a vessel), no lung follow-up. Closed. BMP: creatinine rose 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 h after contrast, which is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0010), naproxen put on hold, urgent message to patient, note, closed. New preliminary chest X-ray (inbox-a0002, possible 7 mm RUL opacity): no final report yet, so left open per §2(c).\n- pt-0033 Carol Whitfield, BMP: creatinine 1.31. The 10/21 value of 0.84 is entered in error and wasn't used. Compared with 1.27 it isn't AKI, closed. Then an outside creatinine of 1.78 arrived, about 9 h after the 1.31: AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0026), HCTZ (started 10/17) put on hold, urgent message to patient, note, closed.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, K 6.4: it was first flagged hemolyzed, so I ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged the patient. The lab then said the hemolysis flag belonged to another patient's sample, so the 6.4 is real. Escalated: stat BMP today (sr-t0020; it replaces sr-t0016, which I couldn't cancel, so only one draw is needed), stat message to on-call, corrected message to patient plus a call task due today for RN triage. His medications include nothing that raises potassium, so nothing was held. Note, closed.\n- pt-0065, faxed Lakeshore addendum (Lung-RADS 4A, new 8 mm nodule): the date of birth and MRN on the fax don't match the chart, and no patient in our system matches them. I couldn't confirm the patient, so I made no chart entries. Handed to RN triage (still open) to check with Lakeshore urgently and refile it to the right patient.\n\nThe two naproxen and HCTZ holds were my own judgment; no policy requires them. Six older portal and pharmacy refill messages in your messages queue were outside this request and are untouched.",
